# Memory & Session Protocol — CodeJudgeX

## Before responding

Read in order (stop when budget hit):

1. `.obsidian-ai-memory/02-PROJECTS/session-continuity.md` — what the last session left off
2. `.obsidian-ai-memory/02-PROJECTS/project-context.md` — stack, constraints, do-not-repeat
3. `.obsidian-ai-memory/02-PROJECTS/active-goals.md` — current priorities
4. `.obsidian-ai-memory/03-ERRORS/error-memory.md` — known bugs, never repeat
5. `.obsidian-ai-memory/03-ERRORS/anti-patterns.md` — never-do patterns
6. Last 1–3 digests in `.obsidian-ai-memory/01-SESSIONS/`

## After meaningful work

Execute all 10 steps in `.cursor/MEMORY-WORKFLOW.md`.

Key steps summary:
- Write digest → `01-SESSIONS/YYYY-MM-DD/session-HHMM-cursor.md`
- Overwrite session-continuity.md (the rolling handoff)
- Code commit + memory commit (always separate)
- Push + include `## Memory` block in final reply
